From: Adam Rice <ricea@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:46:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] [M156] Validate sparse entries before serving any
 request that needs the network

Original change's description:
> Validate sparse entries before serving any request that needs the network
>
> A range request whose first range was cached and fresh skipped
> validation, so the headers were returned to the consumer (and
> original_response_time was left unchanged) before the rest of the range
> was fetched from the network and stitched into the entry. Once the entry
> became contiguous, a subsequent whole-file request could also skip
> validation and serve the modified body under the same
> original_response_time.
>
> Generalise the existing whole-file rule in BeginCacheValidation() to all
> requests: if a sparse entry does not fully cover the requested range,
> validate the first chunk before returning headers. This guarantees that
> a network response (and therefore a new response_time and
> original_response_time) is received and stored before any body bytes can
> come from the network. This is the general case of crbug.com/902724.
>
> As a side effect, a range request that fails conditionalization no
> longer returns the cached prefix twice (crbug.com/40639784).
>
> Update tests that assumed the cached prefix of a longer range request
> was served without validation, and add tests for fresh sparse entries
> and truncated entries.
>
> BUG=580853040,574361804,40639784
